  "contract": "[68BC,68C4) is the next level-setup fragment: BSR 7DB8, BSR 6EF0. 7DB8 returns at once when FF33E2 (two players) is set. Otherwise, when FF31AA is set it clears it and stores D2A2 (\"FRUIT RETURNED!\") in FF0690+46; else it counts FF312C words other than FFFF and, if at least two, stores D28C (\"MIX THOSE FRUIT!\"); either store then calls CB72. CB72 compares the message's leading byte (0x64 for both) with +53 as signed bytes: below it, +46 becomes FFFFFFFF; otherwise +53 takes it and CB9A clears the message row (sets FF010C to 1 for the VDP writes and restores it, register 8004, a VRAM write command for (FF0D60 + 14 + (+56 << 7)) low word, 26 words of 1, register 8014). 6EF0 returns at once unless FF33E2 or FF316C is set; its allocating path (E918 RNG, F9E2 pair) is not reconstructed and rejects natively. CB9A's VDP writes are a logical native request and research-only device effects."
